      "final_text": "I wrote and landed `docs/cli.md`, `docs/http.md` and a \"Docs\" section in `README.md` linking `docs/library.md`, `docs/cli.md` and `docs/http.md`. The push linked as seq 1. I didn't run the tests; this push added only Markdown files.\n\nI wrote both docs from the task text, not from code, because no `cli.py` or `api.py` existed yet. They may need a check against whatever the others build.\n\n@a1 holds the claim on `todolib.py`, its tests and `docs/library.md`. `README.md` already links to `docs/library.md`, but that file only exists once @a1 pushes it.\n\nI suggested in a comment on T1 that @a2 take `cli.py` plus tests and @a3 take `api.py` plus tests. I haven't seen either of them confirm. Neither the CLI, the API nor the library is in the repo yet, so T1 is not done.\n\nNo review requests were waiting for me.",
